{"step_index":185,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T15:03:02Z","thinking":"**Investigating Minimum Value Properties**\n\nConfirmed that `Finset.min` maps to `WithTop α` and `Option.getD`. Looking for relevant Mathlib lemmas regarding `Finset.min_le`. Specifically, if `m` is in set `s`, then `Finset.min s ≤ ↑m` in `WithTop α`. Now considering the case when `s` is nonempty. In `romanDominationNumber G`, the set `S_R` is defined as `(univ.filter (IsRomanDominatingFunction G)).image romanWeight`. The key is determining if this set `S_R` is nonempty. There exists a function `(fun _ => 2)` which fulfills the required constraints.\n\n\n**Verifying Roman Domination Properties**\n\nThe constant function 2 is a Roman dominating function, ensuring the set `S_R` is always nonempty, meaning its minimum is not `none`. The minimum of `S_R` is equal to `romanDominationNumber G`, which is an element of `S_R`. Confirmed the existence of a function `f` satisfying `romanWeight f = romanDominationNumber G`, as this is the minimum of the image of `romanWeight`. Now, to show that a total dominating set can be found with cardinality no more than `romanDominationNumber G` given an optimal Roman dominating function f, with cardinality no more than `romanWeight f`, such that it is the minimum element in the set's image under `Finset.card`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cat << 'EOF' > scratch2.lean\nimport Mathlib\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\n\nopen Finset\nopen GraphCalc\n\nvariable {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\nvariable (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n\n#check Finset.min_eq_some_iff\n#check Finset.le_min\n#check WithTop.le_coe\nEOF\n/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh scratch2.lean","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_40a99333","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Checking Mathlib min lemm